\title{[DC6] Fibonacci recurrence (1 pt)}
\date{2026-10-23T19:02:25Z}
\tag{algorithms}
\tag{problem}

\import{algorithms-macros}

\p{This problem guides you through a derivation of the Fibonacci recurrences in [the previous problem](00Q3).}

\ol{
  \li{Consider the #{2\times 2} matrix ##{M =
      \begin{bmatrix}
        1 & 1 \\ 1 & 0
      \end{bmatrix}.} Compute #{M^2}, #{M^3}, and #{M^4}. What do you notice?}
  \li{State a conjecture about the values of #{M^n} for #{n \geq 1} and prove your conjecture by induction on #{n}.}
  \li{In practice, of course, we could compute #{M^n} using an algorithm like the one in [DC1](00PN). Expand the equation ##{M^{2n} = (M^n)^2} and use it to derive the Fibonacci recurrences in [DC5](00Q3).}
}
